      "message": "Not the biggest fan of passing a Factory here. I might rather inject a factory and then use factory.assertThatVerifier(someUuid). (The factory interface would look different from the Factory you have here.)\n\nActually, on second thought, I\u0027m not sure we want to use Truth here at all. What if we put a method in VerifierOperation that reads the config text? Then your call sites would be:\n\n assertThat(verifierOperations.get(uuid).configText()).contains(...)\n\nIf you want additional operations on the ref other than checking the config text, you can add more methods:\n\n assertThat(verifierOperations.get(uuid).getRefTip()).isEqualTo(someObjectId)\n\nYes, the stuff inside the assertThat(...) isn\u0027t fluent, but is that so bad?",
