      "message": "\u003e Not the biggest fan of passing a Factory here. I might rather inject a\n\u003e factory and then use factory.assertThatVerifier(someUuid). (The factory\n\u003e interface would look different from the Factory you have here.)\n\nHow would it look different?\nI\u0027m interested because we also would need some kind of factory for the assertThatQuery(query).foo syntax that you propose in [1].\n\n[1] https://gerrit-review.googlesource.com/c/gerrit/+/211777/5/javatests/com/google/gerrit/server/query/change/AbstractQueryChangesTest.java#3189\n\n\u003e Actually, on second thought, I\u0027m not sure we want to use Truth here at all.\n\u003e What if we put a method in VerifierOperation that reads the config text?\n\u003e Then your call sites would be:\n\u003e\n\u003e assertThat(verifierOperations.get(uuid).configText()).contains(...)\n\u003e\n\u003e If you want additional operations on the ref other than checking the\n\u003e config text, you can add more methods:\n\u003e\n\u003e assertThat(verifierOperations.get(uuid).getRefTip()).isEqualTo(someObjectId)\n\u003e\n\u003e Yes, the stuff inside the assertThat(...) isn\u0027t fluent, but is that so bad?\n\nLGTM, will do something like this.",
